<div class="hql-hero-grid" markdown>
<div class="hql-hero-text" markdown>

# HQL { .hql-hero }

<p class="hql-tagline">A statically typed expression and query language.</p>

In HQL a type is a data contract. The checker tests a program against its
contracts before it reads any data, and every read tests each record against
them again. One language reads and writes files, PostgreSQL tables, Kafka
topics, NATS subjects, lakehouse tables and HyperMarkDown documents.

<p class="hql-actions" markdown>[[install|Install]]{ .md-button .md-button--primary } [Read the book](/draft/book/){ .md-button }</p>

```sh
cargo install hql
```

</div>
<div class="hql-term" markdown>

=== "Query"

    ```hql
    type Book { title : String, year : Int, rating : Int }

    books = [
        Book(title = "Dune", year = 1965, rating = 5),
        Book(title = "Emma", year = 1815, rating = 3),
        Book(title = "Beloved", year = 1987, rating = 4),
    ]

    books
    | filter(b => b.rating >= 4)
    | sort(b => b.title)
    | map(b => b.title)
    ```

    ```text
    ["Beloved", "Dune"]
    ```

=== "Contract"

    ```hql
    type Book { title : String, year : Int, rating : Int }

    books = [
        Book(title = "Dune", year = 1965, rating = 5),
        Book(title = "Emma", year = "1815", rating = 3),
    ]

    books | map(b => b.title)
    ```

    ```text
    check error[type-mismatch]: `year` of `Book` is Int, and this is String
     --> books.hql:5:33
      |
    5 |     Book(title = "Emma", year = "1815", rating = 3),
      |                                 ^^^^^^
    ```

=== "Kafka → Postgres"

    ```hql
    type EventData : DataContract = {
        id       : Int
        kind     : String
        customer : String
        amount   : Decimal
        at       : String

        require amount >= 0 as non_negative
        require ["order_placed", "order_shipped", "payment_failed"]
            | contains(kind) as known_kind
    }

    type Event    { id : Int, kind : String, customer : String,
                    amount : Decimal, at : String }
    type Rejected { id : Int, message : Data, rules : List<String> }

    tap("order_events_raw")
    | validate(EventData)
    | fork {
        clean =
            oks()
            | map(e => Event(id = e.id, kind = e.kind, customer = e.customer,
                             amount = e.amount, at = e.at))
            | sink("order_clean"),
        quarantine =
            errs()
            | map(e => Rejected(
                id = match e.value.id { some(Int n) => n, _ => 0 },
                message = e.value,
                rules = e.violations | map(v => v.rule)))
            | sink("order_quarantine"),
    }
    ```

    ```text
    order_clean        ids 1, 2, 4, 6
    order_quarantine   id 3  EventData.amount.type
                       id 5  EventData.customer.missing
                       id 7  EventData.non_negative
                       id 8  EventData.known_kind
    ```

=== "Documents"

    ```hql
    cards
    | filter(c => c.metadata.status == "todo")
    | sort(by = c => c.title)
    | map(c => c.title)
    ```

    ```text
    ["Leaves of Grass", "The Common Reader", "The Hobbit"]
    ```

</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="hql-band" markdown>

## One program, end to end { .hql-section }

A source gives values of a type. Each step is checked against that type
before the run. A target receives what the last step gives.

<div class="hql-flow" aria-label="Sources flow through a type contract and a pipeline into targets">
  <div class="hql-flow__stage">
    <p class="hql-flow__label">Sources</p>
    <ul class="hql-flow__chips">
      <li>Kafka topic</li><li>NATS subject</li><li>PostgreSQL table</li>
      <li>JSON file</li><li>HMD vault</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hql-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hql-flow__stage hql-flow__stage--contract">
    <p class="hql-flow__label">Contract</p>
    <p class="hql-flow__code"><code>type EventData : DataContract</code></p>
    <p class="hql-flow__note">checked before the run, enforced on every read</p>
  </div>
  <div class="hql-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hql-flow__stage">
    <p class="hql-flow__label">Pipeline</p>
    <ol class="hql-flow__steps">
      <li><code>validate</code></li><li><code>fork</code></li>
      <li><code>map</code></li><li><code>sink</code></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="hql-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hql-flow__stage">
    <p class="hql-flow__label">Targets</p>
    <ul class="hql-flow__chips">
      <li>PostgreSQL table</li><li>Delta table</li><li>Kafka topic</li>
      <li>file</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="hql-pillars" markdown>

<div markdown>
### Checked before it runs

`hql check` reports a wrong field, type or step with its line and column.
Nothing is read until the program checks.
</div>

<div markdown>
### Batch and stream

`source` reads a table or file whole, as a `Seq<T>`. `tap` reads a topic as
a `Stream<T>`. The same steps apply to both.
</div>

<div markdown>
### Data and documents

A HyperMarkDown vault is a source too: its cards, their metadata and the
links between them are typed values.
</div>

</div>
</section>

<section class="hql-band hql-band--alt" markdown>

## Endpoints { .hql-section }

An endpoint is named in `.hql/config.toml` and used by name in a program.

<div class="hql-endpoints" markdown>

- [**SQLite**](/draft/book/16-tables-and-topics/) <span>table</span>
- [**PostgreSQL**](/draft/book/16-tables-and-topics/) <span>table</span>
- [**Kafka**](/draft/book/16-tables-and-topics/) <span>topic</span>
- [**NATS**](/draft/book/17-subjects-and-the-lakehouse/) <span>subject</span>
- [**JetStream**](/draft/book/17-subjects-and-the-lakehouse/) <span>stream</span>
- [**Delta / Spark**](/draft/book/17-subjects-and-the-lakehouse/) <span>lakehouse</span>
- [**Files**](/draft/book/09-io/) <span>JSON, CSV, text</span>
- [**HMD vault**](/draft/book/21-a-vault/) <span>documents</span>
- [**REST, webhooks**](/draft/book/18-apis-webhooks-and-stores/) <span class="hql-design">design</span>

</div>
</section>

<section class="hql-band" markdown>

## How HQL compares { .hql-section }

<div class="hql-compare" markdown>

|               | What it is                                          | Types over data                                                        | Unbounded streams     | Sources and targets                                             |
| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **HQL**       | Expression and query language, one binary           | Record types are contracts, checked before the run and on every read   | `Stream<T>` beside `Seq<T>` | Files, SQLite, PostgreSQL, Kafka, NATS, Delta, Markdown vaults |
| SQL           | Query language of a relational database             | Column types of the database's tables                                  | Not in standard SQL   | The database it runs in                                         |
| PRQL          | Pipelined query language that compiles to SQL       | Those of the target database                                           | No                    | The database the SQL runs in                                    |
| dbt           | SQL models with Jinja templates, built in a warehouse | Model contracts checked at build; data tests run after               | No                    | One warehouse per target                                        |
| Spark SQL     | SQL and DataFrames on a Spark cluster               | Schemas resolved when a query is analysed on the cluster               | Structured Streaming  | Many connectors                                                 |
| Bend          | General-purpose functional language                 | Not a data language                                                    | —                     | —                                                               |

</div>

Why a language for this, and where it is going:
[An AI-oriented language](/draft/book/00-ai-oriented-language/).

</section>

